---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import AlertBox from '../../components/ui/AlertBox.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/ui/ComparisonTable.astro';
import FAQSection from '../../components/ui/FAQSection.astro';
import ProConBox from '../../components/ui/ProConBox.astro';
import { brands } from '../../data/generator-brands';

const brand = brands.find((b) => b.slug === 'briggs-stratton')!;
const toc = [
  { id: 'status', label: 'Post-2020 status' },
  { id: 'lineup', label: 'PowerProtect lineup' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'Warranty' },
  { id: 'verdict', label: 'Who it suits' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'FAQ' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Briggs & Stratton Standby Generators: PowerProtect Review"
  description="Independent Briggs & Stratton PowerProtect review: post-bankruptcy status, 13–26 kW lineup, 6-to-10-year warranty, Vanguard engines, and dealer reality."
  category="Brands" categoryHref="/brands/" updated="2026-10-03" readingTime="7 min read" toc={toc}
  related={[
    { href: '/brands/generac/', title: 'Generac Standby Generators', description: 'Volume-leader deep dive.', category: 'Brands' },
    { href: '/brands/champion/', title: 'Champion Standby Generators', description: 'Value alternative.', category: 'Brands' },
  ]}
  prev={{ href: '/brands/kohler/', label: 'Kohler Brand Guide' }}
  next={{ href: '/brands/champion/', label: 'Champion Brand Guide' }}
>
  <section id="status"><h2>Post-2020 status: still building generators</h2>
  <p>Briggs &amp; Stratton filed Chapter 11 in <strong>July 2020</strong> and was acquired by KPS Capital Partners (sale completed September 2020), reorganized as Briggs &amp; Stratton Energy Solutions. The standby line survived and was rebuilt as <strong>PowerProtect</strong> — this is not a zombie brand, but confirm your dealer is Energy-Solutions-authorized so parts and warranty flow correctly. <AlertBox type="info" title="Correction note">Some third-party roundups misdate the bankruptcy to 2023. Court records and KPS filings confirm 2020 — one reason to check primary sources, including ours.</AlertBox></p></section>
  <section id="lineup"><h2>PowerProtect lineup (13–26 kW)</h2>
  <ComparisonTable caption="PowerProtect models" headers={['Model', 'Capacity', 'Notes']} rows={brand.models.map((m) => [m.series, m.capacityKw, m.notes ?? '—'])} />
  <p class="mt-3">Vanguard commercial-grade engines, engineered and assembled in the USA, with EnergyTrak 24/7 remote monitoring. Fuel: natural gas or propane.</p></section>
  <section id="warranty"><h2>Warranty: the standout</h2><p>{brand.warranty} Against Generac's tiered 5-year and Kohler's comprehensive 5-year, a 6-year comprehensive standard (and 10-year dealer/DX options) is genuinely class-leading on paper. Read the exclusions and confirm who performs warranty labor in your area before weighting it heavily.</p></section>
  <section id="verdict"><h2>Who PowerProtect suits</h2>
  <ProConBox pros={['6-year comprehensive standard; 10-year options', 'Vanguard commercial engines', 'Competitive mid-range pricing']} cons={['Moderate dealer network — verify local standby service', 'Post-bankruptcy brand confidence varies', 'Fewer published MSRPs; quote variance']} prosTitle="Strengths" consTitle="Watch-outs" />
  <p class="mt-4">Shortlist PowerProtect when a certified local dealer quotes it against Generac/Kohler on identical scope — the warranty is worth real money if service is truly local.</p></section>
  <section id="faq"><span class="sr-only">FAQ anchor</span></section>
  <FAQSection items={[
    { q: 'Is Briggs & Stratton still in business?', a: 'Yes — acquired by KPS Capital Partners out of 2020 bankruptcy and operating as Briggs & Stratton Energy Solutions, still producing PowerProtect standby generators.' },
    { q: 'How good is the PowerProtect warranty?', a: '6-year comprehensive standard with 10-year dealer-exclusive and DX options — among the strongest headline terms in residential standby. Verify current terms and local servicing.' },
    { q: 'PowerProtect vs Generac Guardian?', a: 'Comparable kW bands; Briggs leads on standard warranty length, Generac on dealer density and model choice. Get same-scope quotes and weight dealer responsiveness.' },
  ]} />
  <section id="conclusion"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>A legitimate contender with the best standard warranty in the comparison set — contingent on local dealer strength. Next: <a href="/brands/champion/">Champion</a> or <a href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">installed costs</a>.</p></section>
</ArticleLayout>
